title: May 2022

@may_2022
# prose-audit: Grade A — Tusk's one-list demand and the alternate Kaczyński host-list route now expose who controls candidates, subsidy and programme, with an authored organisational verdict after every answer.
title: The one-list squeeze
face-image: img/poland/events/donald-tusk-2023.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.rates_lists_2022_done = 1;
// The one-list demand is only as strong as KO's claim to be the vehicle. With
// that claim buried in the 2020 first round, the appeal still gets made and
// still gets covered — it simply moves far fewer voters and binds far fewer
// parties.
Q.opposition_list_pressure += Q.ko_hegemony_broken ? 1 : 5;
Q.household_security -= 3;
Q.economic_issue_salience += 5;
Q.tactical_desertion_to_ko += Q.ko_hegemony_broken ? 0.2 : 0.8;
Q.tactical_desertion_to_p2050 += Q.ko_hegemony_broken ? 1.3 : 0.8;
Q.may22_pis_list_route = (
    Number(Q.ko_relation) < 35 &&
    Number(Q.pis_relation) >= 18 &&
    (
        Q.recovery_fund_strategy == "Negotiated PiS deal" ||
        (Q.left_in_government && Q.government_party == "pis")
    )
) ? 1 : 0;
Q.news_headline = Q.may22_pis_list_route
    ? "Rate rises turn Lewica's PiS alignment into an electoral question"
    : "Rate rises and Tusk's list demand squeeze smaller parties";
!}

= May 2022 — The cost of one opposition list

[? if not may22_pis_list_route:
Rising mortgage payments intensify criticism of the government's economic
management. <span class="party-ko"><b>Donald Tusk</b></span>, KO chair and former prime minister, also asks every
opposition party to stand on a single electoral list under a common democratic
argument, forcing Lewica to weigh a cleaner anti-PiS contest against its own
programme, candidates and public subsidy.
[? if ko_hegemony_broken: The appeal is made from a weaker chair than the one
that used to make it. Every party being asked to dissolve into KO's list can
answer with the same number — **[+ ko_2020_r1_share +]%** in the 2020 first
round — and the appeal now has to be argued rather than assumed.?]
?]

[? if may22_pis_list_route:
Rising mortgage payments intensify criticism of the government's economic
management, but our breach with KO has changed the electoral question. KO chair
Donald Tusk's one-list appeal now excludes a Lewica that bargained with, or
entered, Prime Minister Mateusz Morawiecki's governing camp. If that alignment
is to survive an election, PiS chair Jarosław Kaczyński must decide whether his
party list has room for our candidates—and we must decide what accepting his
control would cost.
?]

- @may22_identity
- @may22_front
- @may22_conditions
- @may22_pis_list
- @may22_pis_terms
- @may22_pis_independent

@may22_identity
title: Reject one list and build a recognisable Left alternative
view-if: may22_pis_list_route = 0
on-arrival: party_unity += 3; ko_relation -= 5; p2050_relation -= 1; left_poll_momentum += 0.25; opposition_list_pressure += 2; razem_dissent -= 2; news_headline = "The Left refuses to become a current inside Tusk's list"

Local organisations begin recruiting candidates under Lewica's own name and
Razem welcomes a campaign that will have to state what makes the Left distinct.
Tusk answers that separate lists are a luxury the opposition may discover it
could not afford.

The refusal preserves a political identity, not an electoral guarantee. Every
later poll near the threshold will reopen the argument in more frightened
terms.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@may22_front
title: Accept the democratic-front logic in principle
subtitle: Let Tusk frame the common campaign while reserving the right to negotiate its programme and places.
view-if: may22_pis_list_route = 0
on-arrival: ko_relation += 6; p2050_relation += 3; party_unity -= 4; left_poll_momentum -= 0.15; barons_dissent -= 2; razem_dissent += 6; news_headline = "One opposition list becomes a live negotiation"

Tusk can now present one democratic list as the direction of travel rather than
a KO demand. The SLD apparatus sees safer places inside a larger committee;
Razem asks whether “in principle” has already conceded the name above the
ballot.

Nothing has yet been signed. KO nevertheless enters the negotiation as the
author of unity and Lewica as the party explaining what it still needs.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@may22_conditions
title: Demand programme, Senate and list-place guarantees first
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
view-if: may22_pis_list_route = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No negotiating operation is available.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; ko_relation += 2; p2050_relation += 2; party_unity += 2; public_trust += 1; opposition_list_pressure -= 2; news_headline = "The Left turns one-list rhetoric into written conditions"

Our negotiators put a minimum social programme, Senate coordination, winnable
places and a transparent subsidy formula in one document. KO and Poland 2050
must answer terms rather than ask Lewica to demonstrate virtue by disappearing.

The conditions preserve internal support and cost an organisational month.
They may also give Tusk a ready explanation if the talks fail: the Left priced
unity too highly.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@may22_pis_list
title: Negotiate winnable places on the PiS party list
subtitle: PiS controls nominations and subsidy; the Left carries the governing camp's record into the election.
view-if: may22_pis_list_route = 1
on-arrival: may22_list_strategy = "PiS host-list talks"; pis_relation += 6; ko_relation -= 5; party_unity -= 6; razem_dissent += 10; progressives_dissent += 7; barons_dissent -= 3; coalition_blur += 6; far_right_agenda += 3; opposition_list_pressure -= 3; news_headline = "Lewica asks Kaczyński for winnable places on the PiS list"

Kaczyński's party officers open the candidate books and make the hierarchy
plain: PiS will decide the districts, order and subsidy. The governing camp
gains proof that Lewica's earlier cooperation was not a temporary bargain.

SLD veterans see survivable places. Razem and the progressive current prepare
to campaign against the host list, while KO describes every future Lewica
social demand as an internal dispute inside Kaczyński's bloc.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@may22_pis_terms
title: Demand a social programme, candidate quota and free votes first
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. PiS must put the price of host-list control in writing.
view-if: may22_pis_list_route = 1
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No negotiating operation is available.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; may22_list_strategy = "Conditional PiS host-list talks"; pis_relation += 3; ko_relation -= 3; party_unity -= 2; budget_promises += 2; razem_dissent += 5; progressives_dissent += 3; public_trust += 1; opposition_list_pressure -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica prices PiS list talks with a written social and candidate compact"

Our delegation demands a candidate quota, a written social chapter and free
votes outside it before discussing districts. PiS listens because it values a
broader governing list, but it does not surrender host-party control merely by
receiving the paper.

The conditions make the proposed alliance legible and therefore harder to
hide. Razem still opposes it; voters can at least see what Czarzasty claims the
crossing would purchase.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@may22_pis_independent
title: Break with both hosts and prepare an independent Lewica list
subtitle: Preserve the party's name and programme; relations with both large camps deteriorate.
view-if: may22_pis_list_route = 1
on-arrival: may22_list_strategy = "Independent Lewica list"; party_unity += 4; pis_relation -= 5; ko_relation -= 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.3; opposition_list_pressure += 1; razem_dissent -= 3; progressives_dissent -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica rejects both Tusk's front and Kaczyński's host list"

The party instructs its districts to prepare an independent slate. Members who
feared absorption by either large camp recover a common task and a name they
can put above the office door.

PiS loses the parliamentary ornament it hoped to display; KO loses the claim
to every anti-PiS vote. Lewica inherits the harder responsibility of clearing
the threshold without either host.

- @poland_hub: Continue
